1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,430
Polar research across Antarctica, the Arctic, and the Himalayas generates critical reports, datasets, and media.

2
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:18,860
However, these valuable resources remain distributed across isolated repositories, creating discovery challenges.

3
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:26,910
Smart India Hackathon problem SIH26063 by the Ministry of Earth Sciences calls for an integrated portal:

4
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:34,960
Unifying an archival knowledge repository with an intelligent media dissemination system for public outreach.

5
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:42,050
POLARIS, the Polar Knowledge and Outreach Intelligence System, is our proposed prototype solution,

6
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:49,140
Connecting research archives, structured search, AI discovery, STEM education, and human-governed outreach.

7
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:56,605
Designed for India complete tri-polar scope, POLARIS connects Antarctic stations Maitri and Bharati,

8
00:00:56,605 --> 00:01:04,070
Arctic facilities Himadri and IndARC, and the Himalayan cryosphere at Himansh, linking research with media.

9
00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:11,115
Authorized researchers ingest heterogeneous research resources through a structured pipeline:

10
00:01:11,115 --> 00:01:18,160
Extracting document text, processing legacy scanned logs with OCR, and validating records with FAIR metadata.

11
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:25,230
The processed information is organized within a central repository, combining relational metadata in PostgreSQL,

12
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:32,300
Dense vector representations in pgvector, and raw research media in object storage for auditable preservation.

13
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:39,450
Rather than relying solely on exact keywords, POLARIS combines keyword and semantic search.

14
00:01:39,450 --> 00:01:46,600
When querying Antarctic climate observations, relevant reports, publications, datasets, and photos emerge together.

15
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:53,165
The public discovery layer features an interactive station telemetry and GIS exploration view,

16
00:01:53,165 --> 00:01:59,730
Allowing students and citizens to explore Indian polar stations, historical expeditions, timelines, and verified media.

17
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:07,230
POLAR AI utilizes retrieval-augmented generation to answer scientific inquiries.

18
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:14,730
The system provides evidence-grounded responses, citing exact source documents, expedition years, and report sections.

19
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:20,885
Through the Polar Academy, verified scientific knowledge is transformed into student-friendly explainers,

20
00:02:20,885 --> 00:02:27,040
Interactive cryosphere learning modules, STEM quizzes, and classroom resources for educators.

21
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:33,210
Outreach Studio helps science communicators convert selected research sources into structured drafts

22
00:02:33,210 --> 00:02:39,380
Tailored for official websites, press releases, social media, and student educational portals.

23
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:46,305
Crucially, AI never publishes autonomously. Every generated draft undergoes citation verification

24
00:02:46,305 --> 00:02:53,230
And mandatory review by a human science editor before dissemination, while unapproved drafts return for revision.

25
00:02:53,230 --> 00:02:59,555
From raw field observations and laboratory reports to structured storage, hybrid search, and AI assistance,

26
00:02:59,555 --> 00:03:05,880
POLARIS delivers the complete end-to-end knowledge and science dissemination lifecycle.

27
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:13,450
Key expected outcomes include a unified polar knowledge repository, faster resource discovery,

28
00:03:13,450 --> 00:03:21,020
Traceable AI assistance with citations, accessible STEM education, and controlled institutional science outreach.

29
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:27,800
POLARIS serves researchers seeking cross-expedition datasets, educators teaching climate science,

30
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:34,580
Students discovering polar research, outreach officers crafting verified media, and institutions preserving heritage.

31
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:42,055
The prototype uses proven technologies: Next.js and TypeScript on frontend, FastAPI and Python backend,

32
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:49,530
PostgreSQL and pgvector storage, and containerized Docker deployment, ensuring feasibility and extensibility.

33
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:55,975
Because the platform handles scientific and institutional knowledge, role-based access control,

34
00:03:55,975 --> 00:04:02,420
Cryptographic verification, end-to-end audit logging, and strict human editorial review are built into every workflow.

35
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:09,450
POLARIS is not just a document repository and not an ungrounded chatbot. It is a proposed integrated ecosystem

36
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:16,480
Connecting polar research, verified knowledge, and meaningful outreach for the nation. Thank you.
